        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, thank you for referring this 71-year-old male patient, admitted on 06/01/2012 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Blood gases confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. Spirometry confirmed severe obstructive ventilatory impairment consistent with advanced COPD. Treatment consisted of controlled oxygen therapy, inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids for hydration. The patient responded well, with improved oxygenation and symptom relief. He was discharged on 07/01/2012 in stable condition on optimised inhaler therapy. Please arrange outpatient pulmonology follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
